WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.991
A few numbers make the point.

00:00:04.071 --> 00:00:08.062
Squaring a mixture with K components encodes on the
order of K-squared-over-two pairwise

00:00:08.142 --> 00:00:12.133
components while reusing the same K parameters,

00:00:12.213 --> 00:00:16.204
which is where the compactness comes from,

00:00:16.284 --> 00:00:20.275
and the paper proves this gap over monotonic
circuits is exponential.

00:00:20.355 --> 00:00:24.345
Empirically,

00:00:24.425 --> 00:00:28.416
the squared non-monotonic circuits post the best
test log-likelihoods among tractable models on several UCI datasets,

00:00:28.496 --> 00:00:32.487
for example zero point six two on Power, about
eleven on Gas,

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:36.558
minus twenty point four on Hepmass, and minus
twenty-six point seven on MiniBooNE.

00:00:36.638 --> 00:00:40.629
On the language data they climb toward GPT2's own
likelihood of around minus fifty-two,

00:00:40.709 --> 00:00:44.700
while monotonic circuits flatten out.
